menu "RM67162 panel driver"

config RM67162_USE_LILYGO_SPI_INIT
    bool "Use LilyGO's rm67162_spi_cmd init sequence"
    default n
    help
      The upstream driver sends a minimal init -- SLPOUT, MADCTL, COLMOD,
      WRDISBV -- which brings up the QSPI-wired LilyGO and Waveshare boards it
      was tested on.

      The LilyGO T-Display-S3 AMOLED **Plus** is a different variant: its panel
      is wired for regular SPI and LilyGO's own library drives it with a
      SEPARATE 18-command sequence (rm67162_spi_cmd) rather than the 12-command
      one used for the QSPI boards. Bus width and init sequence are independent,
      so selecting "Regular SPI" alone leaves the panel dark -- the commands
      being sent are the wrong ones.

      Enable this to send LilyGO's SPI sequence instead. Sequence and its
      semantics are from LilyGo-AMOLED-Series (MIT, Lewis He / Shenzhen Xin Yuan
      Electronic Technology).

config RM67162_USE_DC_PIN
    bool "Drive a DC pin (conventional 4-wire SPI)"
    default n
    help
      The upstream transport embeds control bytes in a 32-bit command word and
      uses NO DC pin -- correct for the QSPI-wired boards it was written for.

      The LilyGO Plus is wired for conventional 4-wire SPI: LilyGO's own
      writeCommand() pulls display.d1 (GPIO7) LOW for the command byte and HIGH
      for data. That is a TRANSPORT difference, not an init or bus-width one, so
      no amount of pin or sequence configuration bridges it.

      Enable this to send plain 8-bit commands and let esp_lcd toggle DC. Set
      the panel IO's dc_gpio_num to GPIO7 and lcd_cmd_bits to 8 to match.

endmenu
